<section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><h1>Frequently asked questions</h1><p>Answers to common questions about GEST.</p></div></section><section class="container section content-narrow"><div class="faq-list"><details><summary>How long is the GEST test?</summary><p>Approximately 2 hours and 25 minutes, including Reading (45 min), Listening (35 min), Writing (50 min) and Speaking (approximately 14 min).</p></details><details><summary>How is the overall score calculated?</summary><p>The four skill scores are averaged and rounded to the nearest whole number. There is no pass/fail.</p></details><details><summary>How do I book a test?</summary><p>Register, verify your email address, complete your profile and upload an ID/passport document, then select an available session. Your official photo is taken at the test centre. Your test centre will manage payment confirmation.</p></details><details><summary>How do I receive my result?</summary><p>Your centre enters scores after the test. GEST headquarters reviews the result and publishes a digitally verifiable certificate after approval.</p></details><details><summary>How long is a certificate valid?</summary><p>Normally two years from its issue date, unless the applicable GEST validity policy is updated. A certificate can also be revoked or reissued.</p></details><details><summary>Can a receiving organisation verify my results?</summary><p>Yes. The form number and security code on your certificate are required for public online verification.</p></details><details><summary>Is GEST accepted by every university or visa agency?</summary><p>No. You should confirm that your receiving institution accepts GEST before booking.</p></details></div></section>
